Status: IN_PROGRESS
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoy/issues/89
Milestone: An original soft-glass chime on DS power-on.
Dependencies: 79 separate DS; 87 physical DS power button.
Purpose: Give the DS its own non-chiptune startup identity without replacing
or copying the GBA sound or a manufacturer's startup recording.

Tasks:
- [x] Synthesize an original overlapping sine-partial chime.
- [x] Play only on DS power-on; honor DS mute and clean up its audio context.
- [x] Support real power-on/off with no cartridge, retaining cartridge guidance.
- [x] Qualify rendered audio, physical power routing and mute/error paths.
- [x] Update documentation, tracking and owned continuity.
- [ ] Owner listening/device review.

Acceptance criteria:
The physical DS power switch produces a distinctly different original tune
from GBA. Power-off, ordinary page loads and console selection do not play it.
Muted startup is silent; blocked audio is reported without losing the game.
The existing GBA tune and runtime audio remain unchanged.

Completion evidence:
Syntax,35units and build pass. Final five-case Edge feature gate passes1.6m.
DS offline rendering/physical power case passes6.0s: separate sine partials,
proportional volume, overlapping decay, mute/zero silence, context cleanup,
no selection/off chime, empty-slot power and explicit permission failure.
Existing GBA square-wave startup case passes14.2s unchanged.
Owner listening/device acceptance remains open; numeric checks are not audition.

Completion log:
2026-11-07: Owner requests a separate DS startup sound, explicitly not limited
to an 8-bit style. Use an original soft-glass arpeggio with overlapping decays.
2026-11-07: Offline rendering reveals nonlinear half volume from a fixed
exponential floor; scale it with volume. Wait for scene readiness in audio
fixtures. Keep mute editable without a running cartridge, configuring a native
core only when one exists. Cancel a superseded run before rebuilding dist.
